{
  "$schema": "../../scenario.schema.json",
  "id": "tasks/delegate-task-hands-over-what-its-calling-agent-may-read",
  "title": "delegate_task hands over what both the agent that called and the channel its result goes back to may read: a message for one of them alone stays out; an agent that may not read, or that the room does not bind, hands nothing over; an intelligence channel shared into the child room, which reads the description, stops the hand-over, and a shared transport does not; a host's kit.delegate still reads as the notified channel, and one that may not read is handed nothing",
  "rules": [
    "§23.4",
    "§23.3 step 4",
    "§7.5 rule 1"
  ],
  "notes": "Python: tests/tasks/test_delegate.py; tasks/delegate.py DelegateHandler._do_delegate, tasks/brief.py conversation_block (decided in HITL b5d45a58: access counts on both paths; fcda1b89: a shared intelligence channel stops the hand-over, §7.5 rule 8). A model chooses what it hands over, so the handler reads as the channel whose model chose, and its result goes back to the notified channel, which reads it too. A shared transport receives the worker's answers and changes nothing here, as fcda1b89 says. A host chooses through kit.delegate, whose reader stays the notified channel (§23.3 step 4).",
